Open-source collection of ~5,000 SVG icons - sourced from [Tabler Icons](https://tabler.io/icons),
[Hugeicons](https://hugeicons.com/) and custom designs, normalized and organized into categories.
[Appica icons](https://appica.dev/ui/icons)

<%= embed AppicaUI::IconPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Icon(:star)                                               # outline, 24px, 1.5 stroke
Icon(:star_filled, size: 20, class: "text-warning-emphasis")
Icon("arrow-back-up", stroke_width: 2, aria_label: "Undo")

Button do
  Icon(:download, data: { icon: "start" })
  plain "Export"
end
```

The React package exports one component per icon (`<Star />`); in Phlex a single `AppicaUI::Icon` takes the name. It
renders the same `<svg class="appica-icon">` markup as `@appica/icons-react` - fill/stroke attributes, 24×24
viewBox, `aria-hidden` - with the icon's paths inside. Browse and search every icon in the
[Gallery](<%= Lookbook.previews.find { |preview| preview.preview_class == AppicaUI::IconPreview }.scenarios.find { |scenario| scenario.name == "gallery" }.inspect_path %>) preview; clicking one copies its `Icon(...)` call.

