## Naming

- Every icon has one canonical kebab-case name: `smart-home`, `star-filled`, `sort-0-9`.
- `Icon` also accepts a symbol with underscores (`:smart_home`, `:sort_0_9`) or the React name (`"SmartHome"`).
- An unknown name raises `KeyError` with suggestions ("Did you mean: star?").
- `AppicaUI::IconLibrary.names`, `.categories` and `.each(category)` list the set.

## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `name` | `Symbol`, `String` | - | Required. The icon's catalog name. |
| `size:` | `Integer`, `String` | `24` | Width and height. |
| `stroke_width:` | `Numeric` | `1.5` | Stroke width of outline icons (filled icons ignore it). |
| `color:` | `String` | - | Sets `color`, which `currentColor` follows. |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | - | Name a meaningful icon; it's then `role="img"` instead of `aria-hidden`. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes after `appica-icon`, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Any other attribute goes to the `<svg>`.

## Data & updates

The icons live as JSON in `app/components/appica_ui/icon/icons/` (one file per category plus `index.json`, ~1.7 MB);
a category is read the first time one of its icons renders and then cached. Regenerate them from a newer
`@appica/icons-react` release (no Node needed):

```bash
bundle exec rake "ui_components:icons:sync[1.1.0]"
```

Keep the icon data out of Tailwind's scan in the host app:

```css
@source not "<gem path>/app/components/appica_ui/icon/icons";
```

